WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.250
A researcher asks: do people
remember more words with music,

2
00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:05.660
or in silence?

3
00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:11.350
Plan one: the same people do both tests,
so everyone is compared with themselves.

4
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:14.550
Plan two: split them into
two different groups,

5
00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:16.250
one for each test.

6
00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:17.540
Both sound fair.

7
00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:21.400
So which is better: same
people, or different people?

8
00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:25.650
In this mission, you'll compare designs
where each participant takes part in only

9
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.800
one condition, or in every condition.

10
00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:32.370
You'll meet two ideas every
researcher has to think about:

11
00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:35.490
participant variables and order effects.

12
00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:39.730
And you'll work out how many people each
design needs to collect the same number

13
00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:40.970
of scores.

14
00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:44.830
Your mission: work out which
design is better, and why.
